Hi Karl

I am working with Rqtl and I am trying to do something simple but I don't know how to do that. I want To remove all the individuals with a genotype frequency of the AA genotype above 0.9. Could you please help me with an example to do that?

Best Wishes

--
Eric

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Tue Apr 18 22:44:57 2017
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Tue, 18 Apr 2017 22:44:57 +0000
Subject: Re: remove individuals with a genotype frequency of the AA genotype above 0.9
Message-ID: <H7FkYc0J0G0.m_dUWWyeBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <H7FkYc0J0G0.Mr-Ip1yaBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <H7FkYc0J0G0.Mr-Ip1yaBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/H7FkYc0J0G0/m/m_dUWWyeBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Try this:
# pull out all genotypes as a matrix
g <- pull.geno(mycross)

# frequency of the "1" genotype for each individual
fAA <- rowMeans(g==1, na.rm=TRUE)
# keep only individuals with fAA <= 0.9

mycross_rev <- subset(mycross, ind=(fAA <= 0.9) )

karl

